---
import Hero from "../../components/ds/Hero.astro";
import NotificationBanner from "../../components/ds/NotificationBanner.astro";
import OnThisPage from "../../components/ds/OnThisPage.astro";
import Panel from "../../components/ds/Panel.astro";
import Prose from "../../components/ds/Prose.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE_DEFAULTS } from "../../utils/site";

// This page follows the GOV.UK model accessibility statement:
// https://www.gov.uk/guidance/model-accessibility-statement
//
// Several sentences are LEGALLY REQUIRED and must not be reworded. Lines
// beginning [TODO are facts only the council can supply, and must be completed
// before this statement is published.

const sections = [
	{ id: "how-accessible", label: "How accessible this website is" },
	{ id: "feedback", label: "Feedback and contact information" },
	{ id: "enforcement", label: "Enforcement procedure" },
	{ id: "technical", label: "Technical information" },
	{ id: "non-accessible", label: "Non-accessible content" },
	{ id: "improving", label: "What we're doing to improve accessibility" },
	{ id: "preparation", label: "Preparation of this statement" },
];
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Accessibility statement"
	description="Accessibility statement for the Rotherham Virtual School website."
>
	<Hero
		slot="hero"
		variant="compact"
		title="Accessibility statement for the Rotherham Virtual School website"
		lead="Publishing an accessibility statement is a legal requirement for public sector websites. This draft follows the GOV.UK model statement."
		breadcrumbs={[
			{ label: "Home", href: "/" },
			{ label: "Accessibility statement" },
		]}
	/>

	<NotificationBanner tone="important" label="Draft">
		<p>
			This statement is a draft prepared as part of a prototype and has not been verified,
			reviewed or published. The compliance status, testing details and dates must be
			completed and checked by the council before this page is used.
		</p>
	</NotificationBanner>

	<div class="rvs-two-col">
		<div class="rvs-stack">
			<Prose>
				<p>This accessibility statement applies to the Rotherham Virtual School website.</p>
		<p>
			This website is run by Rotherham Metropolitan Borough Council. We want as many people as
			possible to be able to use this website. For example, that means you should be able to:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>change colours, contrast levels and fonts using browser or device settings</li>
			<li>zoom in up to 400% without the text spilling off the screen</li>
			<li>navigate most of the website using a keyboard or speech recognition software</li>
			<li>
				listen to most of the website using a screen reader (including the most recent
				versions of JAWS, NVDA and VoiceOver)
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			We've also made the website text as simple as possible to understand. <a href="https://mcmw.abilitynet.org.uk/" rel="noopener">AbilityNet</a> has advice on
			making your device easier to use if you have a disability.
		</p>

		<h2 id="how-accessible">How accessible this website is</h2>
		<p>
			[ TODO before publication: summarise the accessibility issues a disabled user can act
			on, in order of most to least impact — for example, sections to avoid, or how to request
			an accessible alternative. If there are none, say so. Do not claim more than has been
			tested. ]
		</p>

		<h2 id="feedback">Feedback and contact information</h2>
		<p>
			If you find any problems not listed on this page or think we're not meeting
			accessibility requirements, contact: <a href={`mailto:${SITE_DEFAULTS.email}`}>{SITE_DEFAULTS.email}</a>.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you need information on this website in a different format like accessible PDF,
			large print, easy read, audio recording or braille:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				email <a href={`mailto:${SITE_DEFAULTS.email}`}>{SITE_DEFAULTS.email}</a>
			</li>
			<li>[ TODO: add a phone number and any other contact route ]</li>
		</ul>
		<p>We'll consider your request and get back to you in [ TODO: number ] days.</p>

		<h2 id="enforcement">Enforcement procedure</h2>
		<p>
			The Equality and Human Rights Commission (EHRC) is responsible for enforcing the Public
			Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2) Accessibility Regulations 2018
			(the 'accessibility regulations'). If you're not happy with how we respond to your
			complaint, <a href="https://www.equalityadvisoryservice.com/" rel="noopener"
				>contact the Equality Advisory and Support Service (EASS)</a
			>.
		</p>

		<h2 id="technical">Technical information about this website's accessibility</h2>
		<p>
			Rotherham Metropolitan Borough Council is committed to making its website accessible, in
			accordance with the Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2)
			Accessibility Regulations 2018.
		</p>

		<h3>Compliance status</h3>
		<p>
			[ TODO before publication: choose one of the legally required options below, delete the
			others, and satisfy yourself that it is accurate. This website has not yet been audited,
			so none of these can currently be stated truthfully. ]
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				(a) This website is fully compliant with the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/" rel="noopener"
					>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines version 2.2</a
				> AA standard.
			</li>
			<li>
				(b) This website is partially compliant with the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/" rel="noopener"
					>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines version 2.2</a
				> AA standard, due to the non-compliances and exemptions listed below.
			</li>
			<li>
				(c) This website is not compliant with the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/" rel="noopener"
					>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines version 2.2</a
				> AA standard. The non-compliances and exemptions are listed below.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="non-accessible">Non-accessible content</h2>
		<p>The content listed below is non-accessible for the following reasons.</p>

		<h3>Non-compliance with the accessibility regulations</h3>
		<p>
			[ TODO before publication: list each problem, the WCAG 2.2 success criterion it fails,
			and when you plan to fix it. Example: "Some images do not have a text alternative, so
			people using a screen reader cannot access the information. This fails WCAG 2.2 success
			criterion 1.1.1 (non-text content). We plan to add text alternatives by [date]." ]
		</p>

		<h3>Disproportionate burden</h3>
		<p>
			[ TODO before publication: list anything you are claiming would be a disproportionate
			burden to fix, with the assessment behind that claim. If nothing, say so. ]
		</p>

		<h3>Content that's not within the scope of the accessibility regulations</h3>
		<p>
			[ TODO before publication: list out-of-scope content, for example PDFs or other
			documents published before 23 September 2018 that are not essential to the service, and
			live video. ]
		</p>

		<h2 id="improving">What we're doing to improve accessibility</h2>
		<p>
			[ TODO before publication: outline the accessibility roadmap, or delete this section. It
			is optional. ]
		</p>

		<h2 id="preparation">Preparation of this accessibility statement</h2>
		<p>This statement was prepared on [ TODO: date ]. It was last reviewed on [ TODO: date ].</p>
		<p>This website was last tested on [ TODO: date ] against the WCAG 2.2 AA standard.</p>
		<p>
			[ TODO before publication: describe how the site was tested and who carried it out — for
			example, automated testing by the website team plus a manual audit by a third party. ]
		</p>
			</Prose>

			<Panel tone="neutral" title="Notes for the council">
				<p>
					The wording in the "Enforcement procedure" and "Technical information" sections, and
					the three compliance status options, are legally required and must not be reworded.
					The statement must be reviewed at least once a year.
				</p>
				<p>
					This draft has not been audited. Automated checks and manual screen-reader testing
					are listed as outstanding items in the project README.
				</p>
			</Panel>
		</div>

		<aside>
			<OnThisPage items={sections} sticky={true} />
		</aside>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
